that you will want to tell your co-worker about or perhaps friend or partner even. Like some of these experiences are so private to us. And we don't really owe anybody the deepest part of ourselves in that way, especially if that's not a safe relationship to make that kind of disclosure in. So I'm thinking of all those people I've spoken to who will say at the office, they just have a made-up story about what they're doing for the holidays, or they have some kind of rehearsed line or two that they will give when people, ask them about their families and what they're doing together. And I think I've heard that so often
以至于我个人反思发现，实际上我对其他人的家庭生活知之甚少。所以我尽量不做假设。因此，我尽量不对我的学生说，比如说，祝你们在家和家人度过一个愉快的夏天。我尽量保持开放的心态，因为我其实并不知道他们会在哪里，或者他们会和谁一起度过时光。当疏离的家庭成员生病或去世时会发生什么？这种事件如何与悲伤相互交织？我认为这是一个极好的问题，就目前已发表的研究而言，我们还没有完全的答案。但我认为，疏离本身当然可以成为一种悲伤、失落和哀恸的经历，

37
00:24:18.000 --> 00:25:09.000
now that I just reflect personally that I actually know very little about other people's family lives. And so I try not to make assumptions. So I try not to say to my students, you know, have a good summer at home with your families, for example. I try and keep that open mind that I don't actually know where they'll be or who they'll be spending time with. What about when an estranged family member gets sick or dies? How does that occurrence interact with grief? I think that's an excellent question that we don't quite have the answer to in terms of published research yet. But I think certainly estrangement itself can be an experience of grief and loss and bereavement.
因此，当家庭成员去世时，这种感觉可能会加剧，因为当时可能没有办法再得到答案、试图修复或弄清楚发生了什么。但我认为疏离家庭成员的去世对某些人来说也可能是一种解脱，因为那种破坏性关系的痛苦和压力不复存在了。

38
00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:38.000
and so that when a family member dies, that could potentially be heightened as there is no way then to perhaps get answers or attempt repair or find out what happened. But I think a death of an estranged family member can also be a relief to some people as well that the pain and the strain of that damaging relationship is no longer existent.
所以我想，这同样很可能会根据个人的经历而有很大差异。听起来在这个心理科学领域还有相当多的未解之题。我只是在想，你现在在研究什么？你想解答的重大问题是什么？还有很多事情需要去做。我特别对人们寻求支持的经历感兴趣。因此，我与人们交谈了解他们的治疗经历的工作，才是我真正希望关注和继续做下去的。也许还可以缩小范围，我认为那会很有帮助。

39
00:25:38.000 --> 00:26:18.000
